     tions return zero on success and non-zero on failure.  In particular, the
     ddeerreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss() will return EBUSY until no more connections
     are using the specified TCP stack.  A module calling
     ddeerreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss() must be prepared to wait until all connections
     have stopped using the specified TCP stack.

EERRRROORRSS
     The rreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss(), rreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss__aass__nnaammee(), and
     rreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss__aass__nnaammeess() functions will fail if:

     [EINVAL]           Any of the members of the _b_l_k argument are set incor‐
                        rectly.

     [ENOMEM]           The function could not allocate memory for its inter‐
                        nal data.

     [EALREADY]         The _b_l_k is already registered or a function block is
                        already registered with the same name.
     Additionally, rreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss__aass__nnaammeess() will fail if:

     [E2BIG]            The number of names pointed to by the _n_u_m___n_a_m_e_s argu‐
                        ment is larger than TCP_FUNCTION_NAME_NUM_MAX.
     The ddeerreeggiisstteerr__ttccpp__ffuunnccttiioonnss() function will fail if:

     [EPERM]            The _b_l_k argument references the kernel's compiled-in
                        default function block.

     [EBUSY]            The function block is still in use by one or more
                        sockets, or is defined as the current default function
                        block.

     [ENOENT]           The _b_l_k argument references a function block that is
                        not currently registered.

